{"ratings":[{"id":"3e54f080403d","clarity":88,"grounding":93,"reasoning":85,"genre_fit":87,"problems":[{"type":"reasoning","quote":"The positive expected value therefore depends heavily on high-scenario upside.","why":"The claim is directionally right, since the central case nets only $52. However, it is not quantified, for example by showing that expected value turns negative if the high-scenario probability drops modestly, so 'heavily' is asserted rather than demonstrated."},{"type":"prose","quote":"I would treat the margin as modest","why":"'The margin' has no clear referent. It could mean the $400 expected net value or the $200 buffer against the loss limit, and the reader cannot tell which."},{"type":"reasoning","quote":"approve expansion for one quarter, with monitoring","why":"The email does not say what monitoring means: no metric, threshold or checkpoint that would trigger stopping. That weakens the conditional recommendation for a decision-maker."}]}]}
